Yes. Since you want to temporarily bypass the real Location BE API and use a hardcoded demo response, you only need to change the Location case in search-autocomplete.component.ts.

1. Add the demo response

Inside SearchAutocompleteComponent, add:

private readonly demoLocationResponse = {
  customerLocations: [
    {
      id: 'LOC001',
      name: 'Pune',
      active: true,
    },
    {
      id: 'LOC002',
      name: 'Mumbai',
      active: false,
    },
    {
      id: 'LOC003',
      name: 'Bangalore',
      active: true,
    },
    {
      id: 'LOC004',
      name: 'Delhi',
      active: false,
    },
    {
      id: 'LOC005',
      name: 'Hyderabad',
      active: true,
    },
  ],
};

You can put it just below:

inputMaxCharacters = 100;


---

2. Replace ONLY the Location case

Currently you have:

case AddPanelType.Location:
  return this.locationService.search(this.searchValue).pipe(
    map((res) =>
      (res?.customerLocations || []).map((loc: any) => ({
        id: loc.id,
        name: loc.name,
        active: loc.active,
      }))
    ),
    switchMap((transformed) => this.handleSearch(of(transformed)))
  );

Temporarily replace it with:

case AddPanelType.Location:
  return of(this.demoLocationResponse).pipe(
    map((res) =>
      (res?.customerLocations || []).map((loc: any) => ({
        id: loc.id,
        name: loc.name,
        active: loc.active,
      }))
    ),
    switchMap((transformed) => this.handleSearch(of(transformed)))
  );

That's it.

3. What happens now

When the selected panel is:

AddPanelType.Location

your flow becomes:

Search "pune"
     ↓
getSearchObservable()
     ↓
AddPanelType.Location
     ↓
demoLocationResponse
     ↓
handleSearch()
     ↓
Autocomplete

It will not call:

this.locationService.search(this.searchValue)

for Location.

Customer and Billing Group are completely untouched and will continue calling their real APIs.


---

4. Demo data behavior

With the demo response:

Pune        active: true   → selectable
Mumbai      active: false  → disabled
Bangalore   active: true   → selectable
Delhi       active: false  → disabled
Hyderabad   active: true   → selectable

If you type m, you'll get Mumbai, but it should be disabled.

If you type p, you'll get Pune, and it should be selectable.


